    <GaugingStation location="Easton Wood" name="West Glen" number="31023">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Ephemeral site installed to gauge a small rural catchment as part of study into recharge of Lincolnshire Limestone.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">There is a 90 degree bend in the channel immediately d/s of the crest. Theoretically rated to 10.7 cumecs. No out of bank flow rating. One peak flow rating across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Flat V weir with crest length of 8.05m. Installed as part of study into recharge of Lincolnshire L'st.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2024 (WINFAP Files v13).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Ephemeral regime. Natural to within 10% at Q95. No abstractions or returns.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Small catchment entirely on Boulder Clay: flows disappear into l'st d/s of gauging station. Rural catchment, mixed farming with significant woodland component.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="QMED contained and should be modular, theoretical rating expected to perform well." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Non-modular flow is not considered by current rating and there are no gaugings to confirm rating." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
